    "body": "Oh, right. `SplitWhitespace` is an iterator, so you aren't supposed to use it from two places.\r\n\r\nThere are two obvious solutions:\r\n1. Stop at the `trim()` when extracting out the common code, and repeat the `split_whitepace()` for each version item.\r\n2. `collect()` after the `split_whitespace()` to materialize in to `Vec<&str>` which can safely be used in multiple places.\r\n\r\nOption 1 is _probably_ more performant, because it doesn't require any allocation, and the strings are quite small.",
    "created_at": "2019-09-26T02:51:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-07T05:19:03Z",
